From: unattributed@example.com
Subject: No Message-ID, no Date, no To header
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit

Some appliances and a surprising number of ticketing systems emit mail
with no Message-ID at all. Storage has to synthesize a stable local
identity for this message, threading has to cope with having nothing to
link on, and the message list has to sort it without a Date. Delivering
the same body twice must not produce two rows with the same synthesized
id, or one row when two were delivered -- whichever rule we pick, this
fixture is where it gets pinned down.
